.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Defines the C-API to the Open Asset Import Library\&. 


.SH "Macro Definition Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "#define AI_ASSIMP_H_INC"

.SS "#define AI_FALSE   0"

.SS "#define AI_TRUE   1"

.SH "Typedef Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "typedef int \fBaiBool\fP"
Our own C boolean type 
.SS "typedef \fBvoid\fP(* aiLogStreamCallback) (const char *, char *)"

.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "\fBASSIMP_API\fP const \fBC_STRUCT\fP \fBaiScene\fP * aiApplyPostProcessing (const \fBC_STRUCT\fP \fBaiScene\fP * pScene, unsigned int pFlags)"
Apply post-processing to an already-imported scene\&.
.PP
This is strictly equivalent to calling \fBaiImportFile()\fP/\fBaiImportFileEx\fP with the same flags\&. However, you can use this separate function to inspect the imported scene first to fine-tune your post-processing setup\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIpScene\fP Scene to work on\&. 
.br
\fIpFlags\fP Provide a bitwise combination of the \fBaiPostProcessSteps\fP flags\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A pointer to the post-processed data\&. Post processing is done in-place, meaning this is still the same \fBaiScene\fP which you passed for pScene\&. However, \fIif\fP post-processing failed, the scene could now be NULL\&. That's quite a rare case, post processing steps are not really designed to 'fail'\&. To be exact, the \fBaiProcess_ValidateDataStructure\fP flag is currently the only post processing step which can actually cause the scene to be reset to NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBASSIMP_API\fP \fBvoid\fP aiAttachLogStream (const \fBC_STRUCT\fP \fBaiLogStream\fP * stream)"
Attach a custom log stream to the libraries' logging system\&.
.PP
Attaching a log stream can slightly reduce \fBAssimp\fP's overall import performance\&. Multiple log-streams can be attached\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIstream\fP Describes the new log stream\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
To ensure proper destruction of the logging system, you need to manually call \fBaiDetachLogStream()\fP on every single log stream you attach\&. Alternatively (for the lazy folks) \fBaiDetachAllLogStreams\fP is provided\&. 
.RE
.PP

