.SS "\fBASSIMP_API\fP const \fBC_STRUCT\fP \fBaiScene\fP * aiImportFileFromMemory (const char * pBuffer, unsigned int pLength, unsigned int pFlags, const char * pHint)"
Reads the given file from a given memory buffer,
.PP
If the call succeeds, the contents of the file are returned as a pointer to an \fBaiScene\fP object\&. The returned data is intended to be read-only, the importer keeps ownership of the data and will destroy it upon destruction\&. If the import fails, NULL is returned\&. A human-readable error description can be retrieved by calling \fBaiGetErrorString()\fP\&. 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIpBuffer\fP Pointer to the file data 
.br
\fIpLength\fP Length of pBuffer, in bytes 
.br
\fIpFlags\fP Optional post processing steps to be executed after a successful import\&. Provide a bitwise combination of the \fBaiPostProcessSteps\fP flags\&. If you wish to inspect the imported scene first in order to fine-tune your post-processing setup, consider to use \fBaiApplyPostProcessing()\fP\&. 
.br
\fIpHint\fP An additional hint to the library\&. If this is a non empty string, the library looks for a loader to support the file extension specified by pHint and passes the file to the first matching loader\&. If this loader is unable to completely the request, the library continues and tries to determine the file format on its own, a task that may or may not be successful\&. Check the return value, and you'll know \&.\&.\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A pointer to the imported data, NULL if the import failed\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
This is a straightforward way to decode models from memory buffers, but it doesn't handle model formats that spread their data across multiple files or even directories\&. Examples include OBJ or MD3, which outsource parts of their material info into external scripts\&. If you need full functionality, provide a custom IOSystem to make \fBAssimp\fP find these files and use the regular \fBaiImportFileEx()\fP/aiImportFileExWithProperties() API\&. 
.RE
.PP

